[N 25-26 Blackfathom Deeps]
[D Forever Warrior 1-30 (Braedyn)\\The Blackfathom Deeps run from the Zoram Strand, with you as the tank: Researching the Corruption, Twilight Falls, In Search of Thaelrid and Blackfathom Villainy, with tank notes, loot calls and the hearth home.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel 25|r  -  you stand on the Zoram Strand in north-west Ashenvale; hearth = Sentinel Hill. This chapter is one dungeon, Blackfathom Deeps: a full clear of 22-28 mobs with bosses at 25-28. Only Thaelrid pays out inside (2,400 XP); the other quests are finished here and handed in later: about 10,650 quest XP in all. Group content: you are the tank - bring a healer and three damage dealers
[OC]|cffffcc00Log check:|r Researching the Corruption (1275, from Auberdine), In Search of Thaelrid (1198) and Twilight Falls (1199) (both from Darnassus). Blackfathom Villainy needs 1198 handed in first, so without 1198 you lose it too
[OC]|cffffcc00Supplies:|r there is no vendor inside, so arrive stocked: food and water for an hour, repair, empty bags
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r Forever's Blackfathom is reported to be Classic's dungeon with only the loot changed. Levels, drops, quests and item stats below come from the Forever DB; boss tactics, locations and the brazier event are Classic-era guide knowledge (Icy Veins, Almar's, Forever guides) and not verified on Forever

[OC]|cffffffffBlackfathom Deeps|r  -  |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r, finder level 15 (Classic figure), mobs 22-28, bosses 25-28, ~60 min. Your quests (only Blackfathom Villainy is picked up inside):
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Researching the Corruption (1275) - 8 Corrupted Brain Stems - |cff66ff66normal|r: nine mob types in the DB drop it (every Fallenroot satyr, Blackfathom Tide Priestess, Oracle, Sea Witch, Myrmidon and Lady Sarevess), so the cave mouth and the first caverns usually cover it; the drop rate itself is not in the DB. Hands in to Gershala in Auberdine (chapter 20)
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r In Search of Thaelrid (1198) - find Argent Guard Thaelrid in an alcove of Ghamoo-ra's chamber - |cff66ff66normal|r, 2,400 XP on the spot, and he gives Blackfathom Villainy
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Blackfathom Villainy (1200) - the Head of Kelris - |cff66ff66normal|r, a quest drop from Twilight Lord Kelris; 3,300 XP at Selgorm in Darnassus (chapter 20)
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Twilight Falls (1199) - 10 Twilight Pendants - |cff66ff66normal|r if you kill every Twilight cultist from the flooded ruins to Kelris (Acolyte, Reaver, Aquamancer, Loreseeker, Shadowmage and Elementalist all drop them; the drop rate is not in the DB, so if you are a few short at the end, go back for the cultists you skipped). 2,550 XP at Manados in Darnassus (chapter 20)
[OC]|cffffcc00Maybe:|r The Heart of the Void (78916, level 25): the DB only knows its end, Selgorm in Darnassus, and its text, "Bring the Blackfathom Pearl". Its giver and the Pearl's source are not in the DB (the three reward items are not in the tooltip service yet either). If a Blackfathom Pearl ever drops, keep it and hand it in at Selgorm with the others; this guide does not track the quest
[OC]|cffffcc00Not for you:|r Baron Aquanis, Amongst the Ruins, Allegiance to the Old Gods, The Essence of Aku'mai and Trouble in the Deeps are Horde quests; Alliance has no sapphire quest

|cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r Gather at the sunken temple on the Zoram Strand and enter Blackfathom Deeps at the cave mouth [G14.5,14.2 Ashenvale]
[OC]|cffffcc00You tank this run|r: Defensive Stance from the first pull, bring a healer and three damage dealers. Pull packs back round a corner so the casters come to you, Thunder Clap when three or more are on you, Taunt anything that turns to the healer, and keep Shield Block for the boss hits. Mark the healers and casters (Tide Priestess, Oracle, Sea Witch) as the first kills
[OC]|cffffcc00The cave mouth|r is held by elites: Fallenroot Satyrs and Blackfathom Tide Priestesses (level 20-21 in the DB; Forever also lists level-25 versions of both, plus Blackfathom Oracles, in the same spot). Pull them in twos, priestesses (healers) first; each one is already a brain-stem chance
[OC]Classic-era: the way in is a swim through a pool at the foot of the ruins and a winding cave of elite naga; the first cavern inside is crossed on stepping stones over water, and falling in sends you back to the start and usually pulls mobs

[OC]|cffffffffThe run|r  -  one long sweep: Ghamoo-ra's chamber, Lady Sarevess to the north-west, the south tunnel to Gelihast and Lorgus Jett, the water section with Old Serra'kis, the temple and Twilight Lord Kelris, the braziers, Aku'mai. Several trash mobs disarm the tank (Classic-era): hold threat with Taunt and Thunder Clap until the weapon is back, and the damage dealers ease off. Caster naga and murlocs (Sea Witch, Tide Priestess, Oracle) cast and heal: kill them first and pull them round corners to you
[OC]|cffffcc00Ghamoo-ra|r (25 elite turtle) in the first big chamber: very high armour, so physical hits do about half damage and the casters do the real work. Face him away from the group; everyone steps out of Trample (random target)
[OC]|cffffcc00Tank (Ghamoo-ra):|r face him away from the group and hold him still; his armour halves physical damage, so the fight is long - Shield Block on cooldown and let the casters do the work
Once the chamber is clear, in the alcove on its south-west side at [TAR4787 Argent Guard Thaelrid], [QT1198] [QA1200 Blackfathom Villainy]
[OC][A Warrior] |cffffcc00Loot (Ghamoo-ra):|r roll on |cff66ff66Spiked Shell Band|r (ring +5 Sta, 4.19% drop); |cff66ff66Tortoise Armor|r (mail chest, 36.96% drop)
[OC]|cffffcc00Lady Sarevess|r (25 elite naga) with two naga guards in the cavern north-west of the chamber, a short swim away: you take all three, one guard dies first, then the other. Forked Lightning is a frontal cone that chains between targets: nobody stacks or stands in front of her. She also casts Slow and Frost Nova, and she drops Corrupted Brain Stems
[OC]|cffffcc00Tank (Sarevess):|r pick up Sarevess and both guards, Taunt the guard the damage dealers are not killing back to you, and turn her so Forked Lightning (frontal cone) points at nobody but you
Keep looting Corrupted Brain Stems - if you are still short here, they keep dropping from every satyr, priestess, sea witch and myrmidon on the way [QC1275]
[OC][A Warrior] |cffffcc00Loot (Lady Sarevess):|r roll on |cff66ff66Darkwater Talwar|r (1H sword 17.1 dps, 38.30% drop); |cff66ff66Naga Battle Gloves|r (leather hands +4 Str +4 Sta, 36.62% drop); |cff66ff66Naga Heartpiercer|r (bow 13.3 dps, 20.46% drop)
[OC][A Warrior] |cffffcc00Loot (Gelihast):|r roll on |cff66ff66Algae Fists|r (mail hands +8 Str +5 Sta, 42.83% drop)
[OC][A Warrior] |cffffcc00Loot (Lorgus Jett):|r roll on |cff66ff66Treacherous Treads|r (mail feet +5 Str +7 Sta, 9.90% drop); |cff66ff66Fallenroot Longbow|r (bow 13.9 dps +2 Agi +4 Sta, 9.96% drop)
[OC][A Warrior] |cffffcc00Loot (Old Serra'kis):|r roll on |cff66ff66Bite of Serra'kis|r (dagger 17.7 dps, 22.66% drop); |cff66ff66Bands of Serra'kis|r (leather wrist +6 Str +3 Sta, 33.41% drop); |cff66ff66Glowing Thresher Cape|r (cloak, 37.86% drop)
[OC]|cffffcc00Gelihast|r (26 elite murloc, skippable for quests, worth it for the Algae Fists) at the end of the south tunnel past Ghamoo-ra. The murlocs round him are the real danger: pull one pack at a time, then pull him alone. His Net roots a random player. Click the stone behind him for Blessing of Blackfathom (Classic-era: +5 Int and +5 Spi, a long buff)
[OC]|cffffcc00Lorgus Jett|r (26 elite, optional): a Horde quest target in the northern tunnel after Gelihast (Classic-era: several possible spawns, so skip him if he is not on your path). Lightning Shield hurts melee - the damage dealers wait for it to drop - and Lightning Bolt on you. The Forever DB gives him Twilight Maul, Treacherous Treads and Fallenroot Longbow (one Forever guide lists only the longbow)
[OC]|cffffcc00Baron Aquanis|r (28 elite): summoned by clicking the Fathom Stone in the water section past the fork, and only the Horde quest cares. Leave the stone alone - he drops nothing for you
[OC]|cffffcc00Old Serra'kis|r (26 elite thresher, skippable for quests, worth it for the loot): in the swim-only cave beside the Baron's stone under the ruins. The whole fight is underwater, so top up breath first (a Water Breathing potion or a caster's buff) and burn him fast; he heals himself every so often, so save a burst for it
[OC]|cffffffffThe temple|r  -  above the water the ruins and the temple are full of Twilight cultists (Acolyte, Reaver, Aquamancer, Loreseeker, Shadowmage, Elementalist: level 24-26 elite casters). They are your pendants, so kill every one. Aquamancers are said to summon water elementals (Classic-era): kill the caster first. Pull casters back to the tank and interrupt
Loot Twilight Pendants from the cultists - if you are short, kill the ones you skipped before you start the braziers [QC1199]
[OC]|cffffcc00Twilight Lord Kelris|r (27 elite warlock) in the ceremonial chamber before Aku'mai's door. He pulls the cultists round him into the fight, so clear the room first. Mind Blast hits hard and Sleep takes a player out: if you are slept, a big threat hit must hold him; dispel the Sleep if you can. Sources disagree on interrupting Mind Blast - try one interrupt and see
[OC]|cffffcc00Tank (Kelris):|r clear the room, then pull him to you. If Sleep lands on you, the damage dealers stop for a few seconds and the healer holds him; Taunt him back the moment you wake
[OC]|cffffcc00Tank (Aku'mai, after the braziers):|r drag him out of every Poison Cloud at once, and use Shield Block through each Frenzied Rage - that is when he kills tanks
Kill Twilight Lord Kelris and loot the Head of Kelris [QC1200]
[OC][A Warrior] |cffffcc00Loot (Twilight Lord Kelris):|r roll on |cff66ff66Twilight Lord Girdle|r (mail waist +8 Str, +6 block value, 3.15% drop); |cff66ff66Wisdom's Leather Helm|r (leather head +13 Sta)
[OC][A Warrior] |cffffcc00Loot (Aku'mai):|r roll on |cff66ff66Stormrider's Leather Helm|r (leather head +13 Sta); |cff66ff66Moss Cinch|r (leather waist +5 Sta, 35.80% drop)
[OC]|cffffcc00The braziers|r (Classic-era: four, round the central statue before Aku'mai's door): click one, kill what it calls (Aku'mai Servants, level 26 elite water elementals in the DB), then light the next. The elementals hit in AoE, so kill one as fast as you can and keep the group together. With all four done the door behind the statue opens
[OC]|cffffcc00Aku'mai|r (28 elite hydra) in the lair behind the statue: Poison Cloud on the ground - pull him out of it and everyone leaves it at once (it can be interrupted); Frenzied Rage (+75% attack speed for about 5 seconds) - Shield Block and defensive cooldowns then, he can kill a full-health tank quickly
[OC]|cffffcc00Trash loot:|r Axe of the Enforcer, Doomspike and Grimclaw (bind on equip, low drop) only if they fall - roll, never farm; Ring of Precision (+6 Agi +3 Spi, unique) for an empty ring slot; the caster staves, Onyx Claymore (2H) and Tree Bark Jacket (cloth) - pass

[OC]|cffffcc00After Aku'mai:|r click the stone behind him for Blessing of Blackfathom if you want it. Nothing hands in down here (Thaelrid was the only inside hand-in), and the Hearthstone works from inside the instance, so there is no walk out
|cFFfff8a3Hearth to [H Sentinel Hill]|r
[OC]|cffffffffHand-ins that wait|r  -  1275 Researching the Corruption: Gershala on the Auberdine dock, at chapter 20's Auberdine pass (the boat is not on your way home). 1200 and 1199: Selgorm and Manados in Darnassus, also chapter 20. Keep all of them in the log
[OC]|cffffcc00Training:|r no trainer on this route. If you skipped your level-24 abilities, they wait for Wu Shen in Stormwind (chapter 15)
[OC]|cffffcc00Check:|r log should hold Researching the Corruption (1275), Twilight Falls (1199) and Blackfathom Villainy (1200), all three completed and waiting for hand-ins, plus The Shieldsmith (1702), Exploring the Alliance (93963) and the carries from chapters 09-12 (1024, 4581, 1035, 1070 and 973 in the plan). Next: walk from Sentinel Hill into Duskwood
[NX 25-26 Duskwood: Darkshire]
]], "Forever Warrior 1-30")
